  <TITLE>Redox Influence on Microbial Communities in Anaerobic Coastal Sediments</TITLE>
  <DESCRIPTION>We inoculated anaerobic sediments from 3 different depths using two different reducing agents (sodium dithionite and titanium (III) citrate) at varied redoxes (-150, -300, -340, -380, and -570mV) over 150 days to assess longterm affects on microbial community composition.</DESCRIPTION>
